// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Root-cause synthesis from all prior attempts:
//
// Best (40.8%): `next == "<<"` missed Qwen's space-prefixed " <<"  token, so
//   effectively ZERO spans were constrained. The 40.8% came from the free LM.
//
// Attempt 60 (0%): Fixed detection with RenderedEndsWith but closed at the
//   very FIRST IsCompletePrefix token — parser considers a single identifier
//   complete, producing <<n>> instead of <<n1 + n2>>. Killed all accuracy.
//
// Attempt 62 (8.2%): RenderedEndsWith + CloseSpanWithinBudget(50). Tracker
//   closes at the LONGEST complete prefix in 50 steps, so the model fills 50
//   constrained tokens with identity operations (*1*1*1, //n//n) before the
//   budget forces the close. Mathematically many neutral, but occasionally
//   introduces non-unit factors (100//10 = 10) that corrupt the answer.
//
// The three failure modes point to a single fix:
//   (a) Detection: use RenderedEndsWith (fix from attempt 62)
//   (b) Minimum token guard before IsCompletePrefix close: prevents <<n>>
//       while still closing well before the repetition loop starts
//   (c) Keep CloseConstrainedSpan-at-first-complete (from best) not
//       CloseSpanWithinBudget(50) (which enabled the repetition loops)
//
// This attempt:
//   1. RenderedEndsWith to detect <<
//   2. Minimum |currentConstrainedOut| >= 3 before closing — skips the
//      single-variable-complete trap but closes as soon as the parser is
//      satisfied after a real multi-token expression (e.g., n1 + n2)
//   3. AdaptiveConstrainedStep inside spans (best's approach)
//   4. CloseSpanWithinBudget with a small 4-step budget only at end-of-budget
//      to fix the four final_span_unclosed syntax failures
//   5. Clean, minimal guidance — no prohibitions that confused the LM
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 — parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Outside-span branch: insideConstrainedOut is false so the implication is
//   vacuous.  EnterObservedConstrainedSpan sets currentConstrainedOut := []
//   and insideConstrainedOut := true; parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by
//   method precondition.
//
//   CloseConstrainedSpan branch (min-token guard satisfied and complete):
//   CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut := false, making the
//   implication vacuously true, and resets currentConstrainedOut := [].
//
//   CloseSpanWithinBudget branch (near budget): postcondition of
//   CloseSpanWithinBudget guarantees
//     insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
//
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep branch: the helper hard-masks to parser-valid
//   next tokens plus EOS, so the returned next token (if not EOS) satisfies
//   IsTokenValidNext(parser, currentConstrainedOut, next). AppendConstrainedToken
//   appends next to both generated and currentConstrainedOut; the
//   IsTokenValidNext guarantee ensures the extended prefix remains parser-valid.
//
// Invariant 2 — progress: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Outside-span branch: steps := steps + 1 and generated grows by at most 1
//   token (EOS path breaks without appending). Invariant preserved.
//
//   CloseConstrainedSpan branch: steps := steps + 1 and CloseConstrainedSpan
//   appends at most one token (">>") to generated. Invariant preserved.
//
//   CloseSpanWithinBudget branch (closeBudget = maxSteps - steps):
//   the postcondition gives |generatedOut| <= |generated| + closeBudget.
//   After steps := maxSteps we have
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + old_steps + closeBudget
//              = |generatedPrefix| + old_steps + (maxSteps - old_steps)
//              = |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps = |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
//
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep branch: steps := steps + 1; AppendConstrainedToken
//   appends exactly one token when next != eosToken; EOS path breaks without
//   appending. In both cases |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
